Preserve the first scenery object's x coordinate when starting a streamed block.

Decrunch_Object_Block@0x430a38 resets the new-stream flag with the original
instruction 430ab8: 66 89 0d 56 93 78 00 (mov WORD [0x789356],cx; cx=0).
The adjacent first scene object's local x is a separate WORD at 0x789358.
Ghidra's int-typed _DAT_00789356 made the reset a DWORD store, zeroing that
coordinate whenever a later block started loading. Patch 405 already corrected
the neighboring window stores at 0x789354, but left this flag store untouched.

Observed in a read-only full original L6 capture at cf260: object 0/0 at
0x7845a0 has the same original shape 0x862154 in both targets, but its local
position@0x789358 is x=15133 in dd2h.exe and x=0 in the port. The object is
then wrongly culled, leaving missing scenery pixels around cf252..270 and
later streaming boundaries. Original clocks, RNG calls, matrix and active
block numbers match. Preserve the exact WORD write; no coordinate injection.

--- a/dd2.c
+++ b/dd2.c
@@ -21436,7 +21436,7 @@
   }
   dec_info = *_level_data + *(int *)(*_level_data + param_1 * 4);
   *(unsigned short *)&_DAT_00789354 = 0x400;  /* asm: word store (flag @0x789356 written separately below) */
-  _DAT_00789356 = 0;
+  *(unsigned short *)&_DAT_00789356 = 0;  /* 0x430ab8: WORD; preserve scene x @0x789358 */
   _decrunch_flag = 1;
   _DAT_0078934c = *(undefined4 *)(&active_object_blocks + param_2 * 4);
   _DAT_0078a15c = param_2;
